			"notes": "Initial release of the mod. Seeking feedback and playtesters. Join the discord if you wish to help!\n\nNo dependencies. Neoforge 1.21.1 only until a stable polished version is released.\n\nIt has a lot of WIP assets, models, textures, translations etc, and although barebones in a lot of areas,  it is playable and has quite a bit to explore already!\n\nFeatures:\n\n- Telescope minigame to search for planets and unlock space travel to them\n- Basic fuel & tank system with minimum requirements for traveling from planet X to Y\n- Super basic rocket takeoff system\n- Astronomy Research Table with unlockable Entries to track your progress and learn more about the planets and it's features!\n- Custom tooltip descriptions on most of the items to add cute bits of lore and immersion\n- Tiny furnitures to collect as rare drops from the planets' puzzles\n\n## **2 Planets to explore**\n\nAsha:\n- Custom Sky & Fog color\n- The overworld equivalent of plains, forest, river & ocean\n- 2 new wood/tree types: Oakroot and Oakheart\n- Oakheart Berries which may grow from Oakheart leaves\n- Custom grass blocks, grass, short grass, and dirt (No unique features compared to vanilla)\n- 5 new Sweetlily Flowers\n- 1 new Lunarveil Flower which lights up the area around it during nighttime\n- 1 new \"block\" of starflies, which light up the area around during night time, and can be collected/moved in a Jar\n- 2 new land mobs: Nimble and Snuffler\n- 2 new fishes: Redtale and Bluetale\n- 1 puzzle structure type (with several variations).\n- Entries are unlockable through solving the puzzle structures, which may drop an entry\n\nLunamar:\n- All biomes are custom, although only Verdure has unique features, being a dense kelp forest.\n- Moonshade Kelp\n- Moonshade Fruit: grows from the kelp and lights up the area around it (With emissive texture for fancy shader support!)\n- 1 puzzle structure type (floating water cubes)\n- 1 new flower, Illuma, that opens up during rain or when underwater \n\ncurseforge - <https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/laicaps>\nmodrinth - <https://modrinth.com/mod/laicaps>\ngithub - <https://github.com/wdiscute/laicaps-neoforge-1.21.1>"
		}
